      "content": "i mean i get the \"complex\" thing, but some of the economists say that moving away from global trade is basically just a step backward for progress. like, isn't the whole point of globalism to make everyone more prosperous by specializing? it feels like if every country just tries to do everything themselves, we're just losing the benefits of being connected. is that a fair way to look at it?",
